  "note": "Poll on Monday 15 May 1939: eleven candidates for nine seats. Labour's challenge left both Unionist members (Martin and Ewart, retiring) defeated, so the council became seven Nationalists and two Labour members. The Northern Whig prints Vincent Mone as \"V. More\"; the Armagh Guardian gives O'Reilly's initial as J. Nominations were taken on Friday 5 May by Patrick Carberry, town clerk."
